==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sga|ga}} {{term|fo|lang=sga}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|ga}} {{term/t|cel-pro|*wo}}, from *''uφo'', from {{etyl|ine-pro|ga}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*upo}}; compare Greek {{term|ὑπό|tr=hupo|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Middle Welsh {{term|go|lang=wlm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Ulster}} {{IPA|[fˠæː]|lang=ga}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep}}

# {{context|Ulster|lang=ga}} [[about]], [[concerning]]

====Usage notes====
The standard Irish and Connacht form {{term|faoi|lang=ga}} (Munster {{term|fé|lang=ga}}) means both "under" and "about, concerning". In Ulster, these two meanings are split: {{term|faoi|lang=ga}} means "under", while '''''fá''''' means "about, concerning".

